{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I have just come from the bath and am writing to you hastily, as the post leaves at 3 o'clock and lunch is approaching. — You can see from the date and the bath taken that I have already advanced about 80 miles and am taking my cure very seriously. — I have first to give you the further report of my journey, which is rather simple. Mr. and Mde Beer will have already told you, before receiving this letter, about the pleasant day we spent together in Cassel, despite the bad weather... The express post only left Cassel on Tuesday evening, so I traveled with a hired coach on Monday the 21st from Cassel to Marburg — without any noteworthy incident; in the evening I was still able to visit Hofrath Suabedissen, Professor of Philosophy, in that bumpy little nest, but he had a whole hedge of female relatives with him, so that I set off again immediately. On Tuesday I drove to Wetzlar, where I first visited Schulz, who lives outside the city in the garden, after dinner; he and his wife had a heartfelt joy over my visit; they are all very healthy and looking well — the children, my godchildren, who were almost sickly, are all very strong and well; the garden is on a hill, and has some buildings lying about 30 steps up the slope; I had to stay with him in the afternoon and evening until 10 o'clock. In the morning Schulz came to me, showed me around the little that was worth seeing, and stayed with me until I boarded the express post at 10 o'clock. — He is with body and soul engaged in very interesting studies; his conversation was very instructive to me; the whole family lives quite happily... Yesterday I arrived in Koblenz at 10 o'clock; the express post from there to Trier leaves already tomorrow; that was too early; I will therefore only depart with it on Monday, — to Trier in one day. Had I been able to calculate it, I could have asked you to write to me in Trier, where I — and that on my birthday — could have received a letter from you; I will drink to your well-being and happiness on that occasion. — Now a heartfelt kiss and greeting, likewise to the boys. In Paris I no longer understand German. — Write to me a lot from Berlin — about you and other things... Greet the friends, Privy Councillor Schulze in particular."}}],"created":1795080668,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":519,"prompt_tokens":650,"total_tokens":1169,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-J2IT4T6OPHEUkQzmgDDqQNOg7EVoBhqf","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":650,"prompt_ms":763.492,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.1746030769230769,"prompt_per_second":851.3514221498065,"predicted_n":519,"predicted_ms":12437.261,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.01015637065637,"predicted_per_second":41.649041537361}}